{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Pennsylvania and Ohio Canal, also known as the P & O Canal, the Cross Cut Canal and the Mahoning Canal was a shipping canal which operated from 1840 until 1877 (though the canal was completely abandoned by 1872).","title":"Pennsylvania and Ohio Canal"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was unique in that it served to connect canals in two states (the Ohio and Erie Canal in Ohio and the Beaver and Erie Canal in Pennsylvania) and was funded by private interests.","title":"Pennsylvania and Ohio Canal"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Erie Canal Harbor (formerly Auditorium until September 1, 2003) is a Buffalo Metro Rail station located in the 100 block of Main Street (just north of Hanover and Scott Streets) next to the South Aud Block of Canalside in the Free Fare Zone, which allows passengers free travel between this station and Fountain Plaza station.","title":"Erie Canal Harbor station"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Passengers continuing past Fountain Plaza are required to provide proof-of-payment.","title":"Erie Canal Harbor station"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Unless there are events occurring at KeyBank Center, in which case Special Events station will be utilized, this is the southern terminus of Metro Rail.","title":"Erie Canal Harbor station"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Since Erie Canal Harbor station serves as a terminal, immediately north is a double crossover.","title":"Erie Canal Harbor station"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Erie Canal Harbor is one of only two stations that are the closest to the Amtrak Exchange Street station located on Exchange Street between Washington and Oak Streets beneath Interstate 190 (the other being Seneca station, located 1,584 feet north).","title":"Erie Canal Harbor station"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: The 17th Street Canal is in New Orleans, Louisiana; the location of the Beaver and Erie Canal is not provided in the evidence.
